With `--type-system-refresh`, `==`, `!=`, `in`, `!in` and prefix equality now accept two values of the same type constructor whose type arguments are comparable component by component at every co- or contravariant parameter, as the legacy resolver does: for example, `(Number, Integer)` and `(Integer, Number)` where both are subtypes of a common trait, or `Pair<A, B>` and `Pair<B, A>` for a datatype `Pair<+X, +Y>` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/47). Non-variant type parameters must still agree exactly, and values with different type constructors, unrelated traits or incomparable components are still rejected. The legacy resolver is unchanged.
